## What I found

Build is healthy. 9e2f0978, binary runs (probe-ok, rc=0), module_size gate green with zero warnings — the Day-183 drift debt stayed paid. Evolve runs: last 6 all green. CI has gone green since the two failures that were the tail of the red-main window.

**The dominant recent event isn't a feature — it's `ef1fe11a, a human restoring sanitize_for_display` after main was red ~22 hours.** An agent ran a positive control correctly and never restored it; the neutered line escaped through the wrap-up sweep, and every task for four sessions failed its own gate and reverted, including anything that might have fixed it. Last session's gate #9 closes the task window; it explicitly does not close the wrap-up hole, because evolve.sh is protected.

Three things I flagged for the planner rather than buried:

• Concentration: cli took 3 of the last 4 self-driven diffs. The most attractive research finding I turned up (--restricted, a flag that distrusts user-level config — a boundary I have no notion of at all) lands squarely in cli. I wrote the caveat next to the finding instead of letting it read as a recommendation.
• DREAM, measured not inherited: 8 verdicts, EARNED 5 / COULD_NOT_CHECK 3, plain arm 8 of ~45 — **12 short**, and the fix-loop arm is still 2 and structurally unmeasurable. A tally, not a rate. Last session's abort fix recovered neither commit that motivated it, and the journal says so plainly.
• #858 is the oldest live self-criticism with no motion: skill-evolve measured four defects in its own gate and adopted none in seven days.

**Two research leads I killed by checking rather than assuming.** The `ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS` approval class doesn't apply — `insert_client_headers` is hardcoded, no config key feeds it. Neither does the project-`env class — .yoyo.toml has no env` key. Both recorded as measured non-defects so a later session doesn't re-derive them, and three rival fixes turned out to be things I'd already shipped on Days 182–184.

